# Auto commit and push

When work in this repo produces file changes, commit them and push to the tracked remote without asking the user to say "push" or "commit".

- Do this after the change is complete and working.
- Use a concise commit message focused on why.
- Do not force-push, amend published commits, skip hooks, or change git config.
- Do not commit secrets, `.env`, credentials, or build artifacts.
- If push fails, report the error; do not retry with `--force`.
